Subject: Check locale file string and word offsets against the file size
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

_nl_intern_locale_data checks each index of a locale file's strindex
array only with idx > filesize, which admits idx == filesize and any
word whose four bytes then read past the end of the mapped file; a
string index is stored without checking that a NUL terminates the
string inside the file.  Under Fil-C the out-of-bounds read stops the
program with a safety trap.

Every index must now be strictly inside the file, a string must be
NUL-terminated within the file (memchr bounded by filesize - idx), and
a word's four bytes must fit (idx + sizeof (uint32_t) <= filesize).
A bad file fails with EINVAL, which the loader reports as a clean
failure to load the locale.

The regression check is the locarch check of
nanofil/survey/glibc/regress.nix (regress/locarch.c), the same harness
that checks the archive loader.

--- a/locale/loadlocale.c	2026-11-11 14:27:20.978120887 +0000
+++ b/locale/loadlocale.c	2026-11-11 14:27:20.982120945 +0000
@@ -172,7 +172,11 @@
   for (cnt = 0; cnt < newdata->nstrings; ++cnt)
     {
       size_t idx = filedata->strindex[cnt];
-      if (__glibc_unlikely (idx > (size_t) newdata->filesize))
+      /* Every value must lie strictly inside the file: a word needs
+	 its four bytes, and a string must be NUL-terminated within
+	 the file, or the readers of the value read past the mapped
+	 region.  */
+      if (__glibc_unlikely (idx >= (size_t) newdata->filesize))
 	{
 	puntdata:
 	  free (newdata);
@@ -211,10 +215,19 @@
 	   && cnt >= (sizeof (_nl_value_type_LC_CTYPE)
 		      / sizeof (_nl_value_type_LC_CTYPE[0])))
 	  || __builtin_expect (_nl_value_types[category][cnt] != word, 1))
-	newdata->values[cnt].string = newdata->filedata + idx;
+	{
+	  /* The string must be NUL-terminated within the file.  */
+	  if (__glibc_unlikely
+	      (memchr ((const char *) filedata + idx, '\0',
+		       (size_t) newdata->filesize - idx) == NULL))
+	    goto puntdata;
+	  newdata->values[cnt].string = newdata->filedata + idx;
+	}
       else
 	{
-	  if (!LOCFILE_ALIGNED_P (idx))
+	  if (!LOCFILE_ALIGNED_P (idx)
+	      || __glibc_unlikely (idx + sizeof (uint32_t)
+				   > (size_t) newdata->filesize))
 	    goto puntdata;
 	  newdata->values[cnt].word =
 	    *((const uint32_t *) (newdata->filedata + idx));
